    <briefdescription>
<para>Build-scoped owner for isolated direct-mode runtimes. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The important constraint here is scope: direct execution may reuse an isolated runtime within one build, but it must not leak that runtime into later builds via daemon-global static state. Gradle shared services give us exactly that lifecycle.</para>
<para>Each cached entry is keyed by the resolved launcher runtime classpath plus the plugin code source. That lets multiple direct tasks in the same build reuse the same isolated classloader when they truly target the same runtime, while still separating builds or runtime changes cleanly. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
